  "notes": "Lab flows are labelled by address: in an attack session every flow to or from 10.10.1.10 gets the attack's label and other flows are dropped; in the benign session every flow is BENIGN. A session whose attack did not exit as expected is an error and contributes no flows. For web_sqli, flows that started before sqlmap (DVWA setup and login) are dropped using a marker webattack.sh prints. 'DoS SYN flood' and 'Web Attack - Sql Injection' are not model classes, so only their family recall is meaningful. with_floor counts a prediction below the 0.5 alert floor as BENIGN, as on the live sensor; no_floor is plain argmax, which is how the test-split scores in reports/week_xgboost.json were computed, so the comparison uses no_floor. exact_class F1 uses only flows whose truth label is a model class and depends on the class mix; recall is the fairer comparison. Family-level macro-F1 is over the families present in the lab data (BENIGN, PortScan, BruteForce, DoS, WebAttack); the test-split macro-F1 is over 14 classes, so the two are not the same measure. The lab has one client and a few services, a round-trip time of about 0.1 ms and flows cut by NFStream at the end of each recording, so timing features differ from CIC-IDS2017's; the repeats of one session are not independent. Lab traffic never entered training, but the lab's attack tools are not the 2017 tools either.",
